  "scope": "Local Windows compatibility diagnostics. The schema comparisons used the existing dedicated-account Jobs through a verified ordinary Medium host. The isolated token experiments used the same ordinary host and an ephemeral zero-capability AppContainer.",
  "finding": "On this Windows build the native bcrypt process-attach path requests write data on the KsecDD device. Schema 5 fails its second, write-restricted access check for that bit. Native status is STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, explicit loading returns Win32 1114, and the Rust image with a static bcrypt import exits with STATUS_DLL_INIT_FAILED before producing its test list.",
  "schema_delta": "Both schema runners set DISABLE_MAX_PRIVILEGE, LUA_TOKEN and WRITE_RESTRICTED (0x0d). Schema 4 includes its dedicated account and Everyone among the restricting SIDs. Schema 5 combines a zero-capability AppContainer with one private writer as the sole restricting SID. The device grants the write-data bit to Everyone. Its discretionary ACL contains no ACE for that private writer.",
